    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d216">

                <pb facs="0396" n="324" xml:id="pg324"/>

                <head>No. 161.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Frelinghuysen to Mr. West</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1882-06-19"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 19,
                        1882</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Referring to previous correspondence in relation to the incursions of Canadian
                    Indians into the territory of this country, I now have the honor to inform you
                    that, having received intelligence to the effect that Big Bear, with five
                    hundred lodges of Cree Indians, intends to cross the border into Montana
                    Territory during the present month for the purpose of hunting, the President has
                    instructed the proper officer to warn “Big Bear,” in that event, to return to
                    Canada, and, if he shall disregard the warning, to take the necessary military
                    measures to enforce his return.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>FRED’K T. FRELINGHUYSEN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
